{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Hilbert-Samuel Polynomial.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Hilbert-Samuel Polynomial.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"hilbert samuel polynomial hilbert samuel polynomial","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Hilbert-Samuel Polynomial.md","fileName":"Hilbert-Samuel Polynomial.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Hilbert-Samuel Polynomial","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 20:05\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Associated Primes and Module Dimension]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Associated Primes and Module Dimension","Dimension of a Module","Hilbert-Samuel Multiplicity","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Hilbert-Samuel Polynomial.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Hilbert-Samuel Polynomial.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"hilbert samuel polynomial hilbert samuel polynomial","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Hilbert-Samuel Polynomial.md","fileName":"Hilbert-Samuel Polynomial.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Hilbert-Samuel Polynomial","heading":"Hilbert-Samuel Polynomial","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"For an ideal of definition I in a Noetherian local ring and a finite module M, the length ℓ(M/IⁿM) agrees with a polynomial in n for all sufficiently large n. This is the Hilbert-Samuel polynomial.\n\nIts degree is the [[Dimension of a Module]]. Its leading coefficient, after normalization by a factorial, defines the [[Hilbert-Samuel Multiplicity]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Associated Primes and Module Dimension","Dimension of a Module","Hilbert-Samuel Multiplicity","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Hilbert-Samuel Polynomial.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Hilbert-Samuel Polynomial.md","sourceType":"markdo